WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.330
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.290
"Ikebukuro West Gate Park"

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.500
I've never rented the same porno twice.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.120
Yes, you have.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.580
This is the third time.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:50.750
Nope.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.540
How much must I like it...

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.540
I like it...

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.580
Uh, what is it again?

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.080
Cut!

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:05.500
The line is: "How much must I like it
to rent it three times?!"

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.410
This isn't easy.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.540
You're not used to it, so it's
no wonder you forget your lines.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.950
Work on your acting. Your delivery's
got to be more natural.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.000
I <i>am </i>being natural.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.950
Don't pretend to be nice, just be natural.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.120
"Pretend to be nice?!"

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.750
Okay! Take 6!

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:23.250
Take 6!

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.200
"Camera, Don't Roar!!"

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:32.540
At the time, I was wrapped up
in some outrageous trouble.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:36.830
I was acting in an independent film.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:40.040
This is Toshiaki, the film's director,
and a clerk at a rental shop,

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.250
which is like an endangered species
in this golden age of streaming.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:48.080
"Rental"                        "All 1F items are ¥100 rentals"

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:48.080
When the owner told Toshiaki
he can use the shop for whatever,

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.580
"Rental"                        "All 1F items are ¥100 rentals"

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.580
as they're going out of business soon,
he made the bet of his life.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.500
"Camera, Don't Roar!!"

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:55.910
He scraped together 5,000,000
from credit-card loans here and there,

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:58.500
wrote a screenplay and found a crew,

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:03.540
and asked me to perform because
he reads my column a lot, or something.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:06.540
That's when he said this with a straight face:

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.700
"My life won't amount to much anyway.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:13.410
So just this once, I'm going
to shoot a movie I like."

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.910
Five-minute break!

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:22.330
I was a fool to carelessly sign on to his dream.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.870
Makoto-san, good work.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.160
Oh. Incidentally, this is Crow.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:31.040
He's a G-Boys kid who's a big-time movie fan.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.700
Damn, though. Acting's hard.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:36.910
Huh? But you did really well in there.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:39.660
Crow, you're a nice guy.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.290
No, I was being serious.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.700
Did you hear what happened last night?

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.200
Nothing more than rumor.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.830
What happened?

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:55.290
In our... Hiroto faction,
there's a team called Yamato Gale.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.660
They were attacked.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.080
They're tough fighters,
but they still got messed up.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.370
Who did it?

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:05.000
It was dark, and they were
wearing animal masks...

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.540
I hear there were several of them, though.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:11.370
One of them was calling themselves "Shadow."

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.790
Shadow? Was there a team
like that in the G-Boys?

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:18.750
No. And so, Hiroto-san said...

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:24.290
Well, he suggested it might have
been King who set up the attack.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.000
Takashi? No way.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.950
Hiroto-san has had an axe
to grind with King for a while.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:35.580
Like, he means to take his place someday.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:40.540
So maybe King's noticed,
and this was him issuing a warning.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.580
I'm worried.

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.660
It could mean war, at this rate.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:46.620
Never...

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.290
We're ready.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.450
Let's film some more.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.620
Once we're done here, I'll give Takashi a call.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:57.950
Seriously?

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.410
This is the fifth time.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:15.660
For real?

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:18.500
The titles are similar, but subtly different.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.870
Gotcha.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:25.040
Huh? The title's different,
but it's the same actress.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.500
Oh, by the way! Have you
heard of Mayuna Serizawa?!

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.000
Cut!

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.660
Okay! Much better than yesterday!

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.250
Just call me the "you can do it if you try" kid.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:43.080
That one's always over there.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.950
Don't you ever change up the angle?

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:48.250
That's for the making-of feature,
so it's always running.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:51.750
You're even shooting a making-of?
For a self-made film?

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.830
Sure, it's once in a lifetime.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:06:59.620
What is it?

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.870
Another one of our teams was attacked.

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:03.120
By Shadow?

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:08.120
I went by the hospital earlier,
and it's so bad, they're unrecognizable.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.540
Did you get in touch with King?

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:14.500
No. I called several times,
but he didn't answer.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.660
This really isn't good.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.120
At this rate, a war really will--

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.620
We've got to avoid that no matter what.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:25.290
Actually, Makoto-san.
Hiroto-san wants to meet with you.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.950
Are you free tonight?

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:32.500
I've got to step out for a bit.
Shoot some other scenes.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.410
Hey! That's a problem!

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.870
Hey, Saru? Can we meet up right now?

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:49.160
Makoto, if you call me up
with a bunch of questions,

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.950
hurry and pay me that money.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.830
Huh? What money?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:57.370
Don't play dumb with me.
August 31st, eighth grade!

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.830
Who was it that did
no homework over summer break,

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:05.200
then came crying to me
to help him for ¥500, huh?!

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.200
¥500.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.790
When are you talking about?

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.910
So, have you gotten ahold of anything?

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.700
Don't underestimate the
PR head of the Hidaka Group.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.790
You must mean these teams of kids
who keep getting beat up.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:21.160
It's making my boss nervous, too.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:24.620
The head of the Hidaka Group? Why?

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.790
Balance.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:30.450
For the most part, we keep
the Ikebukuro underworld in check.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.330
Even Donglong, who recently joined
forces with a Kansai organization,

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:37.700
is keeping quiet these days now that
a big boss in Shanghai is eyeing them.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:43.660
But as I'm sure I don't have to tell you,
Ikebukuro has more than an underworld.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.080
There are a hell of a lot of gray zones.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:51.500
It's the G-Boys who are overwhelmingly
strong, within those zones.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:56.410
If each of the teams is a kingdom,
that makes the G-Boys a federation of kingdoms.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.330
In other words, an empire.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:04.250
And the empire's #1 is King--Takashi.
That's how it works.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:07.080
If it's an empire, he wouldn't
be King. He'd be Emperor.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.370
Never mind the details!

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:16.120
Anyway, it's safe to say the underworld
and the G-Boys hold Ikebukuro in balance.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.830
And their relationship ain't bad these days.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:25.080
But you know, Hidaka-san is always
sensitive to this world's balance.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:30.290
If the kids go and start a war,
that balance will...

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:37.620
Did you find out anything about Shadow?

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:40.450
That's what I want to know the most.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:42.450
Shadow, huh?

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:48.500
Seems Shadow is the highest-ranking
go-getter in the underworld.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:53.540
Does jobs for extraordinarily high fees.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:56.830
I don't even know if it's
an individual or a group.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:05.700
For a totally unknown identity,
"Shadow" is a fitting name.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.500
There's somebody like that out there?

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.950
The underworld is abuzz.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:13.750
There's no doubt that Shadow
has come to this town.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.200
You don't suppose Takashi hired Shadow, do you?

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.830
Takashi doesn't do things like that.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.250
Then who did?

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:25.040
Oh, maybe those Red-whatevers who've
been hanging out lately at East Gate Park?

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:29.120
Red Angels. I doubt they'd
do such a thing, either.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.540
So, who <i>did</i>?

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.080
Someone with a grudge against Takashi?

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:36.790
Good luck narrowing down
a list that freaking long.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:39.790
What about Takashi? Hasn't he said anything?

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:41.830
No, nothing.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:43.660
Thanks a lot, Saru.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.700
Makoto, you're not in the G-Boys!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:49.700
If you don't know where to draw
the line, you'll be in trouble.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:52.870
I just want to stop the war.

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:57.160
You've never listened to what I say, anyway.

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:59.950
You're dealing with Shadow.

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:02.790
Be careful you don't get killed.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:06.540
Sure, Saru.

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:10.370
I can't have you dying
before I snatch that ¥500.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.910
How about <i>you </i>die, stupid?

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:17.620
Be careful, Makoto.

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:21.660
That jerk! He didn't leave
any money for his coffee!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:34.000
"Episode 6"
"G-Boys Winter War, Part 1"

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:40.410
Makoto-san.

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:42.330
Knight awaits you.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.500
Knight?

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:51.290
Stop right there.

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:59.250
Hiroto. You're making them call you "Knight"?

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:04.660
I'm surprised. The teams in my faction
make up 30% of the G-Boys.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:09.120
The chances of just my guys
getting attacked over and over is...

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.500
Isn't it a little hard
to call this a coincidence?

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:19.290
But we still don't know exactly who's behind it.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:22.410
It might be some kid
who has a grudge against you.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:24.450
You've seen a lot of stuff in your time.

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:28.500
Yeah. Not as much as Takashi, though.

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:33.500
Did you know? Shadow is a freelance hit man.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.330
First I've heard of it.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:38.450
Takashi wouldn't hire someone
as dangerous as that.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.500
--So, there's no proof he's
trying to take down your fac--

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:43.790
--That doesn't matter!
--So, there's no proof he's
trying to take down your fac--

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:50.080
I've been waiting so long for the day
someone pulls the trigger at us.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:56.160
It doesn't matter who pulls it,
or what form the incoming bullet takes.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:59.120
Just so long as it gets pulled.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:02.450
Wait, don't you want to know the truth, too?

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:05.750
I'll be sure to find out
who the attackers really are.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:08.500
Promise me you won't do anything until then.

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:09.620
All right.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:14.700
But the next time my teams get attacked,
I won't consider it a coincidence.

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:19.660
That's when there'll be war amongst the G-Boys.

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:22.620
You think you can go to war
with Takashi and win?

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:26.250
I won't go easy the way he does!

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:29.660
The G-Boys can handle doing bigger things.

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:33.580
They could even take command
of all the kids in Tokyo!

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:37.660
Makoto, we're only 30%, but we're fighters.

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:39.750
"Don't underestimate us."

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:44.200
Tell that to Takashi.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:50.700
Shit! What makes <i>him </i>Knight?!

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.500
Hiroto-san!

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.370
--Knight!
--Is it finally time?!

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:58.700
We're ready anytime!

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:00.910
--We've got this!
--We'll do it!

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:08.870
"Takashi"
"Dialing"

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:08.870
Great...

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:11.750
In that case...

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.290
Sorry to call you here so suddenly.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.500
Makoto-san, we know
the situation for the most part.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.330
You couldn't possibly think it's us...

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:27.660
I want to hear firsthand
about that "possibly" part.

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:29.910
Straight from Kyouichi.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:36.000
We're not involved.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.250
That's the truth?

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:40.080
You doubt me? That makes me sad.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:44.620
Didn't we work together
to bring down OK Holdings?

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:47.660
We have no reason to wage war.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:51.790
I wouldn't want to expose
my guys to danger in the process.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:56.370
All right. Sorry to make
you say that weird stuff.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:58.500
However...

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:03.580
If sparks should come flying our way,
we <i>will </i>have to brush them off.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:08.620
Sparks fly easily, in war.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:11.330
Let's say...

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:14.870
...something happens where
we bleed even a single drop.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.700
We'll show no mercy.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:19.330
"Takashi"

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.080
What's wrong?

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:26.580
Funny you should ask! I just got followed
by somebody who seemed hella dangerous!

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.660
You've heard the Shadow rumors, right?

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:30.450
Yeah. But why follow you?

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:31.950
How should I know?!

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:35.120
But at least pick up when I call!

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:38.790
I figured Hiroto would do this someday.

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:43.950
He has a lot going for him,
but he lacks experience.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:47.370
And he doesn't have a good partner.
That makes him different from me.

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.790
"Ma La Xing Fu"

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.790
[Spicy Happiness]

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:50.620
Oh! Spicy, spi--

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:53.160
"Ma La Xing Fu"

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:53.160
[Spicy Happiness]

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:58.040
With all this mess going on,
why didn't you call me at all?

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:03.290
Because someone extremely dangerous
like Shadow is prowling around this town.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:06.450
I didn't want to get you involved.

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:09.410
Because I don't know
whether I can keep you safe.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:11.620
Don't underestimate me, Takashi.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:14.660
Keep talking, and I'll punch even you.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:19.250
What do you think I am?

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:21.370
I only hang out when things are safe,

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:23.950
then don't lend a hand when
something dangerous happens?

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:27.620
That's the kind of man you thought I was?

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:30.790
I'm too stupid to know much about friendship.

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:34.660
But we take the truly dangerous risks together,

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:37.620
and we also take the big-ass losses together!

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.080
That's what buddies do!

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:46.000
How many people do you have
whom you can truly rely on?

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.330
Don't underestimate me, Takashi!

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:52.580
You are a bona fide idiot.

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:56.370
You're an idiot, but you're also my buddy.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:18:01.830
Anyone else saying those words would
make me sick, but this is just how you are.

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:04.580
So, I might as well have you help.

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:07.660
Find out Shadow's whereabouts and true identity.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:10.910
Just drag the shadow out into the bright light.

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:12.080
And after that?

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:16.660
If they're really that good,
I'd like to go up against them.

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:19.450
Man, you sure are something.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:23.160
Until we know the truth, don't make
any moves against the Hiroto faction.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.660
Promise me.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.330
Sure.

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:33.160
Never tell the G-Boys kids I shook your hand.

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.750
If you do, I'll leave your skull so messed up,

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:38.870
you won't be able to tell its original shape.

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:40.910
Yes, yes, Your Majesty.

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:44.370
I won't say a single word
to your entire retinue.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:48.660
Uncultured remarks like that fit you perfectly.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:57.750
What?!

00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:01.330
Some more of Hiroto's guys
got jumped. In West Ikebukuro!

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:05.910
Some Donglong guys were attacked
in a Chinese restaurant called Xing Fu.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.200
Donglong?!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.120
From here, Xing Fu is closer. Come on!

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:32.620
Makoto! Where're you wandering around at?!

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:35.910
I want to go ahead and shoot
the night scenes, so come back!

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:38.000
Y-Yeah, sorry.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:39.540
Right now, I'm...

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:46.620
I'll call you back!

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:50.620
Crow, thanks for filling me in earlier.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:52.750
--What's wro--
--This way, King.

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.750
Hey Takashi!

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:08.750
Another one of my teams just got jumped.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:09.790
I know.

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:11.450
I bet.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:17.040
Of course you would, when you're sending
Shadow around and laughing about it.

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:20.910
Hey, Hiroto. Takashi didn't hire Shadow.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:25.830
The rumors say it costs a hell of a lot.

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:27.910
This town has lots of rich people,

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:31.660
but you're the only one
who'd profit from crushing me.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:37.040
If you want to go from being Knight
to King, use your head a little more.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:39.250
This time, Donglong was attacked.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:42.910
They're not the G-Boys. How do you explain that?

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:44.910
How should I know?!

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:49.370
Anyway, three of my teams
got messed up really bad.

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:55.450
Tonight, a beast calling itself Shadow
is prowling around Ikebukuro.

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:59.540
A beast hired by somebody
who wants the G-Boys to go to war.

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:05.200
But now that they've also made a move
against Donglong, things get messy.

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:10.410
Someone wants to completely
wreck the balance in this town.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:15.410
And that someone is well
aware of our weak points.

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:18.370
That's you, Hiroto.

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:22.120
If possible, I want to avoid any bloodshed.

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:23.790
Cool your head a little.

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:26.080
There's plenty of bloodshed already.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:31.040
Takashi also promised not to mess
with you guys until we know the truth.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.120
So, calm down!

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:36.080
I'll track down Shadow, and whoever hired them.

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:36.500
--Until then--

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:38.250
--After tonight, I'm out of the G-Boys!
--Until then--

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.410
--After tonight, I'm out of the G-Boys!

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:46.500
I won't take orders from you anymore.

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:50.410
Starting tomorrow, I'm making my own plans!

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.250
You got that, Takashi?

00:21:57.870 --> 00:21:59.370
Wait, Hiroto!

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:02.620
The war's already started!

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:20.000
<i>What's up</i>

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:23.120
<i>A world where guys with plans</i>
<i>are the first to fade away</i>

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:25.830
<i>The thought hit me after being out all night</i>

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:28.660
<i>A gulf forms with the respectable types</i>

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:31.790
<i>The MIC you nervously gripped</i>

00:22:31.790 --> 00:22:34.410
<i>Leave it behind on the stage</i>

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:37.500
<i>Unable to trust in the next move</i>

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:40.450
<i>You get down off the stage of dreams</i>

00:22:40.450 --> 00:22:43.250
<i>Fade away from the bustle of the scene</i>

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:46.160
<i>Do you know what becomes of him after that?</i>

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:49.290
<i>In fact, are you even prepared to know?</i>

00:22:49.290 --> 00:22:52.040
<i>Now that we're involved,</i>
<i>I want to watch you take off</i>

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:54.790
<i>From the runway you chose</i>

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:58.790
<i>If we happen to meet again today or tomorrow</i>

00:22:58.790 --> 00:23:02.450
<i>Somewhere on this Earth</i>

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:03.910
<i>Let's have fun freestyling</i>

00:23:03.910 --> 00:23:07.000
<i>Like we did that time</i>

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:09.660
<i>What's up</i>

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:11.160
<i>After the live show</i>

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:12.660
<i>In a train window</i>

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:14.040
<i>A brother's face, I find</i>

00:23:14.040 --> 00:23:15.540
<i>Comes suddenly to mind</i>

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:18.540
<i>Right now, I don't feel like</i>
<i>lookin' back on the past</i>

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:21.410
<i>But no way in hell am I forgettin' it</i>

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:22.870
<i>After the live show</i>

00:23:22.870 --> 00:23:24.370
<i>In a train window</i>

00:23:24.370 --> 00:23:25.790
<i>A brother's face, I find</i>

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:27.250
<i>Comes suddenly to mind</i>

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:30.160
<i>Right now, I don't feel like</i>
<i>lookin' back on the past</i>

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:33.500
<i>But no way in hell am I forgettin' it</i>
